WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.693
Step 1. Open the observation definitions list.

1.2
00:00:03.693 --> 00:00:06.836
Here you change an observation definition,

1.3
00:00:06.836 --> 00:00:10.204
or retire one that staff must not pick again.

1.4
00:00:10.204 --> 00:00:15.194
In Settings, under Clinical, select Observation Definitions.

2.1
00:00:15.194 --> 00:00:20.861
Step 2. Find the observation definition. Type its title in Search definitions.

2.2
00:00:20.861 --> 00:00:24.402
To see observation definitions with another status,

2.3
00:00:24.402 --> 00:00:27.680
select that status in the Status filter.

3.1
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:33.772
Step 3. Open the edit form. In the row of the observation definition, select Edit.

3.2
00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:37.191
Care opens the Edit Observation Definition form,

3.3
00:00:37.191 --> 00:00:40.683
with the same sections as the create form.

4.1
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:46.067
Step 4. Change the details and save. Change the fields, then select Save.

4.2
00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:50.005
Care does not change the slug when you change the title,

4.3
00:00:50.005 --> 00:00:53.108
and opens the page of the definition.

5.1
00:00:53.108 --> 00:00:56.630
Step 5. Retire the observation definition.

5.2
00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:02.864
If you are not on its page, select View in its row. Select Delete, then Confirm.

5.3
00:01:02.864 --> 00:01:05.857
Care sets its status to Retired.

6.1
00:01:05.857 --> 00:01:10.672
Step 6. Make a retired observation definition Active again.

6.2
00:01:10.672 --> 00:01:14.927
In the Status filter, select Retired, then select Edit.

6.3
00:01:14.927 --> 00:01:18.177
In Status, select Active, and select Save.

6.4
00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:23.628
Activity definitions and diagnostic reports then offer it again.
